    "result": "Perfect! The frai-core test suite is now fully passing. All 28 tests across 8 test files are passing.\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed two issues in the frai-core package:\n\n1. **`src/finetune/index.js`**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`. The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export but it was only available in the default export.\n\n2. **`src/eval/metrics.js`**: Changed `toxicityMetric` function signature from accepting `bannedTerms` as a second parameter to only accepting `outputs`. Previously, when `runEvaluations` called the metric with both outputs and references, the references array was being incorrectly used as banned terms, causing test strings like \"hello\" and \"friendly world\" to be flagged as toxic.\n\nAll public exports remain intact and functional.",
